  "description": "WOYFEX crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C66 H76 Cl2 Mn2 N6 O22 Tb4,8(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 3 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.557-3.985 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.11-111.65°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [{LMn(Cl)(μ3-OH)Tb2(μ3-OH)(μ-Piv)2}2]·8MeCN. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
